      "name": "Petra",
      "description": "Carved directly into rose-red sandstone in what is now southern Jordan, the ancient city of Petra served as the capital of the Nabataean Kingdom from the 4th century BC to 106 AD when its history was ended by the annexation into the Roman Empire. The iconic facades of Ed-Deir and especially Al-Khazneh demonstrate the impressive skills of the ancient peoples inhabiting the region. ",
