      "id": "Wonder_Capital_Alhambra",
      "code": "A",
      "name": "Alhambra",
      "description": "Built on a hilltop plateau overlooking Granada, this palace and fortress represents the final flowering of Islamic architecture in Europe. Constructed primarily between 1238-1358 by the Nasrid dynasty, the Alhambra served as the seat of government during the final centuries of Al-Andalus. After the Christian conquest of Granada in 1492, it became a royal palace for Spanish monarchs. Having fallen into neglect in the 18th and early 19th century, the complex has been later restored to its former glory.",
