      "code": "CC",
      "name": "Cité de Carcassonne",
      "description": "Cité de Carcassonne remains one of most complete examples of a medieval European fortified city. Located in southern France it represents 13th-century military architecture, with its double walls and 52 towers. Originally fortified by Romans, then expanded under the Trencavel family, Carcassonne played an important role during the Albigensian Crusade when it served as a Cathar stronghold. The 3-kilometer circuit of walls protected the castle and a community of artisans, merchants, and nobles.",
