      "description": "Construction of the white marble bell tower began in 1173 but was nearly immediately affected by the soft clay soil that would make it world-famous. The tower began tilting during construction of the second floor, forcing architects to compensate by building subsequent floors with one side taller than the other. The greatest recorded tilt of about 5.5 degrees has been later reduced to 3.97 degrees to prevent the tower's collapse. This architectural accident became one of Italy's most recognizable landmarks. ",
